  <heading>CFLTLS (register)</heading>
  <desc>
    <brief>
      <para>Compare registers and fault if lower than or same</para>
    </brief>
    <authored>
      <para>This instruction compares the values in two registers, and
generates a Conditional fault exception if the first value is lower than or the same as the second.
If an exception is generated, the <syntax>&lt;reason&gt;</syntax> operand
  is copied to <xref linkend="ESR_ELx">ESR_ELx</xref>.</para>
      <para>This instruction does not affect the condition flags.</para>
    </authored>
  </desc>
